  "stage": "synthesis-review",
  "summary": "I could recover both interpretations from the Year B concise study before comparing it with the expansive study. One asks how God gives a sinner the will to pray and do justice, the other what work the ascended Christ entrusts to a gifted household. The inventory, four overview rows and developed comparisons are present. In the rendered chronology, the Mark 13:33\u201337 row pairs Jesus\u2019 charge on Mount Olivet opposite the Temple with c. A.D. 29, explicitly derived and disputed as to the Passion date. The next two rows give separate composition estimates. No print export was requested. Comparison with Jerome on Isaiah, Augustine and Bellarmine on the Psalms, Chrysostom and Thomas on Paul, Bede on Mark and the U.S. liturgical books disclosed two qualifications the concise study needs to restore."
}
